                <pb facs="0537" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg529"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/3170: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Walton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-08-28T20:00:00-04:00">August 28, 1941—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>51 [bis]. The contents of your despatch 646 of July 10 have been received with
                    great interest. Please inform the Department by telegraph whether any of the
                    trade practices referred to, excluding the matter of navicerts, are still in
                    effect. You should in the future report incidents of this kind by telegraph.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
